From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: mediatek: disable software role switch after init failure

The MT6878 graph can be probed before its remote USB role-switch device is
available. Do not leave software_role_switch set when initialization fails:
the power-on path would otherwise queue an uninitialized delayed_work item.
The PHY remains usable in its default device role.

--- a/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-tphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-tphy.c
@@ -941,9 +941,11 @@ static void u2_phy_instance_init(struct mtk_tphy *tphy,
 	int ret;
 
 	if (instance->software_role_switch) {
 		ret = u2_phy_software_role_switch_init(instance);
-		if (ret)
+		if (ret) {
 			dev_warn(&instance->phy->dev, "failed to initialize role switching\n");
+			instance->software_role_switch = false;
+		}
 	}
 
 	/* switch to USB function, and enable usb pll */
